## Open Questions

1. **Post-Call Summaries:** Standard Telegram bot summaries can be static (reading variables from state) or they can be generated dynamically using a quick background call to the LLM when the phone call drops. Generating dynamically gives a better summary of *that specific call*, but takes an extra second. Which approach do you prefer: static reading of saved mistakes, or generating a fresh custom summary using the latest conversation history?
2. **Handling Early Hangup:** The instructions tell the agent to do a recap when the user "tries to hang up before the end". Do users typically indicate "I have to leave" verbally, or simply cut the phone call abruptly? (If they cut abruptly, the agent cannot verbally recap, but the Telegram text summary will still catch them).

